{
	"_comment": "The lands of the continent, and how the ground of each is generated (src/chronicle/biome.gd picks one per tile; src/area/ground_gen.gd lays it out). Art for every land but grassland and forest is a recoloured stand-in from tools/recolour_biomes.py (docs/22-asset-provenance.md). Densities are props per cell; features are how many of each kind of patch a ground gets on average. `foes` are who camps in a land: a band there draws from them `land_foe_share` of the time and from the faction that walks the terrain otherwise (src/chronicle/encounter.gd). `effects` are what the land does to the party (src/chronicle/biome.gd, `Biome.effects`). `edge_band` is how many cells of the next land's floor run into a tile where two lands meet (D128, the edge sheets from tools/draw_edges.py). `life` scales how many birds, butterflies, bees and other small things a land's tiles get (world_rules.json → life, D179; 1 when absent).",
